# The llama.cpp build that ships inside CherryColaLLM's packages.
# Vulkan builds: they run on NVIDIA, AMD and Intel graphics through the
# normal graphics driver, and fall back to the CPU (with the best CPU
# backend for the processor) when there is no usable GPU. CUDA builds are
# NVIDIA-only and need ~400 MB more, so people who want one install it
# themselves; one on PATH wins over the bundled copy.
# To update: pick a tag from https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases,
# then fill in the two sha256 sums (sha256sum of each downloaded file).
LLAMACPP_TAG=b12800
LLAMACPP_LINUX_SHA256=daac51e306d5522f9f75d95d7fbb4469adfb523816edf118eacef479e857e5ae
LLAMACPP_WINDOWS_SHA256=8b1aa9a8d4c025850608a066167cbab9651d5c38a6db08133a47ef2a000eda90
